README: Lab 3 Pi Mission Control

---Setup Requirements---

    Directory: You must be inside the lab3 folder for data logging to work correctly. If you run scripts from the root directory, data files will be created in the wrong locations.

    Configuration: Before flight, ensure flight_state_machine.py and log_to_terminal.py have simulate = False.

---How to Launch---

The launch.py script automates the opening of three essential terminal windows.

    Open launch.py and set SIM_MODE = True for testing on a laptop, or False for hardware/real testing.

    Run the venv:
    'activate' once inside the venv/Scripts/ folder

    'python launch.py'

---Component Overview---

    Flight State Machine (flight_state_machine.py):

        The core mission loop running at 10Hz.

        Polls IMU and Temperature sensors.

        Logs binary data to the data or simulated-data folder using CCSDS format.

    Ground Station Dashboard (log_to_terminal.py):

        Provides a live text-based UI of current sensor values.

        Monitors system status and warns if temperatures exceed 50°C.

    Active Plotter (active_plot.py):

        A live-updating dashboard that refreshes every 10 seconds.

        Displays four scatter plots: Accelerometer, Gyroscope, Magnetometer, and Temperatures.

Data Analysis & Filtering

To analyze specific datasets without running the full mission loop, use plot.py with date tags.

Note: On Windows, you must wrap date arguments in double quotes to handle the | character.

    To plot a specific time range:

    python plot.py --minDate="02/03/2026|21:30:00" --maxDate="02/03/2026|22:00:00"

    To plot simulation data:

    python plot.py --simulate

Interrupting & Safety

    Exit: Press Ctrl+C in any terminal to stop the process.

    Cleanup: The flight_state_machine.py will automatically perform a GPIO.cleanup() upon a keyboard interrupt to protect the Raspberry Pi pins.

